{title: Camptown Races}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{c: Verse 1}
The [G]Camptown ladies sing this song, doo-dah, doo-dah,
The [G]Camptown racetrack five miles long, [D7]oh, doo-dah day.

{c: Verse 2}
I [G]come down there with my hat caved in, doo-dah, doo-dah,
I [G]go back home with a pocket full of tin, [D7]oh, doo-dah day.

{c: Chorus}
[C]Going to run all [G]night, going to run all day,
I [G]bet my money on the bobtail nag, [D7]somebody bet on the [G]bay.
